---
// MethodologyNote.astro — pure static explanation of the NEB GPA methodology.
// No client JS and no calculator logic (Requirement 1.3, 21.2, 23.3).
// Key message: GPA is computed by weighting GRADE POINTS, not raw marks.
---

<section id="methodology" class="border-b border-hairline bg-canvas-soft">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
      How the GPA is calculated
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-mute">
      The official NEB SEE GPA weights grade points, not raw marks. Here is the
      exact process this calculator follows.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-mute">Step 1</span>
        <h3 class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-ink">Marks become a percentage</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          Theory and practical are handled separately. Each component's marks are
          converted to a percentage of its own maximum.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-mute">Step 2</span>
        <h3 class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-ink">Percentage maps to a grade band</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          Each percentage falls into a discrete grade band on the SEE 4.0 scale,
          and every band carries a fixed grade point — for example A+ is 4.0.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-mute">Step 3</span>
        <h3 class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-ink">Subject GP is a weighted average</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          A subject's grade point is the weighted average of its component
          <em>grade points</em>: theory and practical at 75/25 for standard
          subjects, or 50/50 for Computer Science. Raw marks are never averaged.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-mute">Step 4</span>
        <h3 class="mt-1 text-base font-semibold text-ink">Final GPA is credit-hour weighted</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The final GPA is the credit-hour-weighted average of every subject's
          grade point: the sum of (credit hours × subject GP) divided by the sum
          of credit hours.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-3 text-sm text-body">
      <span class="font-semibold text-ink">In short:</span> grade points are
      weighted, never raw marks. This matches the official NEB marksheet exactly.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
